    <channel>
        <title>DuoUpdater</title>
        <!--
          The Sparkle feed. `scripts/publish-release.sh` regenerates this file on
          every release and pushes it here. The app reads it through
          https://updates.duoupdater.app/appcast.xml (workers/appcast relays this
          file); builds before that read
          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/main/appcast.xml
          directly, so this path must keep working.

          Deliberately empty rather than absent: an appcast with no items means
          "nothing newer available", which Sparkle handles as up-to-date, whereas
          a missing file is a fetch error on every check. The first release fills
          it in.

          Release history starts here. Earlier builds were published from a
          separate binary-only repo that existed only while the source was
          private, and are not carried over.
        -->
        <item>
            <title>0.5.27</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:31:31 +0800</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/jizhi0v0/duo-updater/releases/tag/v0.5.27</link>
            <sparkle:version>157</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.27</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[**Docker Desktop updates follow the Stable or Nightly channel you select in Docker.** Update checks for Stable work again.

**Alfred 6 can check for updates on its stable and preview channels.** Alfred 5 still receives its own updates and links to the official Alfred 6 migration guide when the upgrade is available.

**IntelliJ IDEA EAP stays on the EAP update track.** Update checks account for the licensing requirements of JetBrains preview builds.

**TestFlight apps stay in the TestFlight group** even when a beta build is incompatible with your Mac.

**Update handling is more reliable for GitHub Desktop, DSH NEXT, Bitwarden OSS, and UTM.** This covers the official GitHub Desktop installer, DSH NEXT’s new Apple Silicon package, Bitwarden OSS edition matching, and republished UTM builds.

**VMPal release notes are available again.**
]]></description>
